How can elevator sheet metal processing companies grasp the dividends of the elevator market?
In the 1990s, elevator sheet metal processing plants basically used multi-station punching machines to process plates, which required a lot of molds. The complex mold design was very time-consuming and labor-intensive, and it had high requirements for operators, resulting in expensive labor, long production cycles, and costs.
With the rapid development of laser technology, medium and low-power industrial-grade laser cutting machines have been supplied to the market on a large scale. Domestic laser cutting machine manufacturers are contending, and equipment prices have fallen.
The application of laser cutting machine in elevator sheet metal processing can greatly improve processing efficiency and quality, shorten the manufacturing cycle of new products, reduce labor intensity and processing costs, and create greater economic benefits for enterprises.
