Hi, I am Robert and am 31 years-old and I live in Lubbock, Texas. I have always been fascinated by tools and appliances.
This is why I joined Tools Doctor as a researcher and reviewer. The sad fact is that the tools and appliances market is full of fake, substandard and counterfeit products.
Does it accomplish the purpose for which someone would buy it?
This looks at aspects like installation, operation, maintenance, and cleaning. A product which requires genius-level intelligence to operate may not be of much use to an ordinary person – irrespective of how functional it is.
This answers the question: does the product deliver accurate results, consistently?
For instance, if a tool is supposed to be built according to certain certification standards, an accurate tool is one which meets those specifications. If an appliance is supposed to heat up to a certain specified temperature, it is accurate when it reaches the temperature.
For how long can you count on it to serve its purpose?
Value for Money
