For parts with large machining allowances, in order to have better heat dissipation conditions during processing and avoid heat concentration, symmetrical processing should be used during processing. If a 90mm thick sheet needs to be machined to 60mm, if one side is milled, the other side is milled immediately, and the flatness is 5mm once; if repeated feeding is used for symmetrical processing, each side is processed twice.
If there are multiple cavities on the plate parts, it is not appropriate to use the sequential processing method of one cavity and one cavity during processing. This will easily cause uneven parts to be deformed.
