Coping Tips from COVID Support VT Featured in Burlington Free Press With Covid restrictions lifting throughout Vermont, re-entry is on everyone’s minds. For many of us, re-engagement brings mixed emotions.
SIGN UP HERE FOR MAY 24 TOWN HALL ON RETURNING TO WORK
How do we bring our best selves to the job in the midst of an ongoing pandemic and the uncertainties it brings?
Navigating returning to the workforce is the focus of a virtual Town Hall May 24 from COVID Support VT, in partnership with Mercy Connections. Billed as a “post-Covid confidence builder for employment seekers,” the Town Hall will explore how to connect with our strengths and bring positivity into our efforts around re-joining the workforce.
Heather Gilbert, the self-development coordinator at Mercy, will lead the 1.5-hour interactive session. Participants will learn how to apply a strength-based perspective to planning their next steps for returning to work.
