The outdoor environment poses low risk for Covid transmission. Families should feel comfortable participating in outdoor activities,” Bell said in an email.
Tips for a Covid-Safe Halloween The American Academy of Pediatrics’ safety tips for Halloween can be summarized as “Think Outside” and “Mask Up Inside.” Some general guidelines.
Dress accordingly in layers; use reflective tape and light colors for visibility.
Inside and outside, practice safe distancing between others. Avoid clusters of children gathered at doorways, for example.
Remind kids to wash up thoroughly before partaking of their haul.
Encourage your kids to use their face masks as part of their costume (think surgeon or superhero!).
Staying outdoors with children is the best bet for a safe and fun Halloween
