Seven Days Features Story of Bennington Group Home Caregivers’ Loyalty and Determination Under Covid Lockdown - COVID Support VT
The story of Randy and Gatling House serves as an example of how Vermont’s professional caregivers are going above and beyond the call of duty as the pandemic slogs on. It’s a caregiver’s worst nightmare.
One of the residents is Randy, a 72-year-old man with “a gentle soul” who was blind, noverbal and had a severe intellectual disability. Randy has lived at Gatling House for a decade.
He was placed in hospice and not expected to live long. Even though she was herself suffering symptoms of Covid, Hede and other staff refused to abandon their posts at the home.
