Laparoscopic surgeries in Thailand is performed as a diagnostic and therapeutic procedure, primarily in the abdominal and pelvic area of the body. Although many other less invasive methods of diagnosis exist, such as ultrasound procedures, CT scans, and MRI scans, sometimes these methods don’t provide doctors with the information that allows them to treat the specific problem.
The instrument that allows doctors to see inside the body in real-time is called a laparoscope. It’s a long, thin tool with a handle at one hand that’s inserted through an incision in the abdomen or in the pelvic area and manipulated by a skilled doctor.
Unlike the flexible endoscope, which is used to provide a video image of the hollow visceral organ of the body, a laparoscope is rigid. The doctor is able to target the specific area of the abdomen that he suspects is the source of the problem.
Some uses of laparoscopic surgery are in the diagnosis and treatment of problems with the appendix, gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, liver, small intestine and the stomach. The laparoscope is also used in the pelvic region and reproductive organs of the body and thyroid surgery.
There are several hospitals around Thailand that are equipped to offer laparoscopic surgery. But one of the best qualified and equipped hospitals, in doctors, staff and equipment, is Vejthani Hospital in Bangkok, Thailand.
After the diagnosis afforded by laparoscopic surgery, the talented doctors at Vejthani Hospital will be in the best position to offer state-of-the-art treatment for any condition the diagnosis reveals.
