Poor quality of the carbonizer will cause significant losses to the casting enterprise. The adverse effects after adding molten iron mainly include the following:
The absorption is slow and the absorption rate is low, which results in high power consumption and increased cost;
Many slags lead to increased use of slag removers, causing unnecessary waste;
Other harmful elements affect the quality of molten iron, castings may become defective/non-conforming products, which is difficult to accept and cause losses.
According to different cast iron products and different proportions of ingredients, it can be divided into adding carbonizer before, middle and later of electric furnace, adding steel scrap at the same time and adding late in melting. Among them, the joining step in the later stage of smelting is the most important and can play the role of pretreatment.
